@{ ViewData["Title"] = T["Privacy & data"]; }
<article class="policy-page">
    <div class="page-header"><span class="eyebrow">@T["YOUR INFORMATION. YOUR CHOICE."]</span><h1>@T["Privacy & data"]</h1><p>@T["How this application handles rider profiles and emergency reports."]</p></div>
    <div class="alert alert-warning">@T["This is a technical privacy summary for the MVP. The operator must complete the controller details, legal bases, processor agreements and privacy notice before using the service with real riders."]</div>
    <section class="card"><h2>@T["What is collected"]</h2><p>@T["Your account contains your email address and login information. Your rider profile may contain identification, health details, instructions, a photo and emergency contacts that you choose to provide. Health information requires explicit consent before it is saved."]</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>@T["What a sticker scan reveals"]</h2><p>@T["A QR or NFC sticker contains a random URL, not medical information. Anyone with that URL, including someone who photographs your sticker, can view the fields you choose to publish. Medical fields are private by default. The profile preview lets you check the shared information. Deactivating or replacing the sticker stops future access through that identifier."]</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>@T["Accident reports and location"]</h2><p>@T["Opening a profile does not report an accident or request location. A helper must explicitly submit a possible accident report. Browser location is requested only after the helper chooses to share it. Reporting remains available if location permission is denied. Reports are unverified and do not contact public emergency dispatch systems."]</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>@T["Notifications and incident access"]</h2><p>@T["Confirmed contacts can receive an email invitation for a possible accident report. Invitation links are private, revocable and time limited. Each link grants access to that incident only. Email delivery information means queued, accepted by the mail server, or failed; it does not prove that a person read the message. Do not forward an incident invitation to people who should not have access."]</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>@T["Keeping data secure"]</h2><p>@T["Account and administration pages require authentication and authorization. Public identifiers use random tokens. Administrators manage account status and limited incident metadata; the normal administration interface does not display medical profiles. Production operation requires HTTPS, protected encryption keys, encrypted database storage and backups, and restricted operator access. Sensitive operations are audited without placing medical contents in logs."]</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>@T["Retention and your choices"]</h2><p>@T["You can edit your details, withdraw health-data consent, change visibility, remove contacts, revoke stickers, export your account data or request account deletion from your profile. Incident, notification and audit retention are configured by the operator and displayed in administration settings. Expired incident access is refused, and scheduled cleanup removes retained records according to those settings. Backup retention must be documented separately by the production operator."]</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>@T["Cookies and outside services"]</h2><p>@T["The application uses necessary authentication, request-security and language-preference cookies. Its interface assets are hosted locally, with no advertising or analytics trackers included. Email uses the operator's configured mail service. Opening a map link or initiating a telephone call invokes the service or device you choose. Continuous location tracking and an external AI service are not part of this MVP."]</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>@T["Contact the operator"]</h2><p>@T["Before production launch, the operator must publish their identity, privacy contact, applicable retention periods, rights-request procedure and supervisory-authority information. This technical summary does not certify GDPR compliance."]</p></section>
    <a href="/profile" class="btn btn-primary">@T["Manage my data"] <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
</article>
